{"explanation":"Add instrumented coverage using the preserved EncryptedKey public API. The tests verify encoded-key and algorithm-name recovery after direct and Gson-serialized round trips, and verify that encrypting identical material twice under one AES key creates distinct persisted records while both remain decryptable. All encryption/decryption tests retain GeneralSecurityException and IOException declarations so checked Cipher failures propagate to the Android test runner.","review_assumptions":["EncryptedKey's persisted record representation is Gson-compatible, as required for the serialized-record coverage; successfully decrypting a Gson round-trip proves that the persisted cipher transformation, encoded AlgorithmParameters, ciphertext, and plaintext-key algorithm/AAD selector are retained.","The provided production API surface exposes no MasterKey encryption output or usable Encryptor key-acquisition entry point, and the coordinated production contracts keep both provenance paths unchanged pending the required CrySL trace. This test therefore exercises the common EncryptedKey entry point rather than inventing unsupported provenance-path APIs.","No immutable pre-change serialized fixture or EncryptedKey field/constructor API was supplied. The serialized round-trip test is the equivalent compatibility coverage supported by the retained persisted-record contract; manual review should add a fixed historical fixture if one is available from deployed data.","Different JSON records for repeated encryption of the same plaintext under the same key are the observable representation of separately prepared random GCM parameters/nonces. A nonce collision is cryptographically negligible."],"no_change_required":false,"decision":"MULTI_FILE_FIX_PROPOSED_FOR_REVIEW","confidence":"medium","edits":[{"source_file_path":"mobile/src/androidTest/java/org/fedorahosted/freeotp/EncryptedKeyTest.java","original_code":"package org.fedorahosted.freeotp;

import androidx.test.runner.AndroidJUnit4;
import junit.framework.TestCase;

import org.fedorahosted.freeotp.encryptor.EncryptedKey;
import org.junit.Assert;
import org.junit.Test;
import org.junit.runner.RunWith;

import java.io.IOException;
import java.nio.charset.StandardCharsets;
import java.security.GeneralSecurityException;
import java.security.NoSuchAlgorithmException;

import javax.crypto.KeyGenerator;
import javax.crypto.SecretKey;
import javax.crypto.spec.SecretKeySpec;

@RunWith(AndroidJUnit4.class)
public class EncryptedKeyTest extends TestCase {
    private SecretKey generateKey(String algorithm) throws NoSuchAlgorithmException {
        KeyGenerator kg = KeyGenerator.getInstance(algorithm);
        kg.init(256);
        return kg.generateKey();
    }

    @Test
    public void test() throws GeneralSecurityException, IOException {
        SecretKey tok = generateKey("HmacSHA512");
        SecretKey key = generateKey("AES");

        EncryptedKey ek = EncryptedKey.encrypt(key, tok);
        SecretKey res = ek.decrypt(key);

        Assert.assertArrayEquals(tok.getEncoded(), res.getEncoded());
        assertEquals(tok.getAlgorithm(), res.getAlgorithm());
    }

    @Test
    public void testUTF8() throws GeneralSecurityException, IOException {
        String plaintxt = "火尸木火1十寥日烤";
        SecretKey key = generateKey("AES");

        byte[] plaintxt_encoded = plaintxt.getBytes();

        SecretKey plaintxt_key = new SecretKeySpec(plaintxt_encoded, "AES");
        EncryptedKey ek = EncryptedKey.encrypt(key, plaintxt_key);

        SecretKey sk = ek.decrypt(key);
        byte[] decryptedBytes = sk.getEncoded();
        String decryptedText = new String(decryptedBytes, StandardCharsets.UTF_8);

        assertEquals(plaintxt, decryptedText);
    }
}
","edit_kind":"test","corrected_code":"package org.fedorahosted.freeotp;

import androidx.test.runner.AndroidJUnit4;
import com.google.gson.Gson;
import junit.framework.TestCase;

import org.fedorahosted.freeotp.encryptor.EncryptedKey;
import org.junit.Assert;
import org.junit.Test;
import org.junit.runner.RunWith;

import java.io.IOException;
import java.nio.charset.StandardCharsets;
import java.security.GeneralSecurityException;
import java.security.NoSuchAlgorithmException;

import javax.crypto.KeyGenerator;
import javax.crypto.SecretKey;
import javax.crypto.spec.SecretKeySpec;

@RunWith(AndroidJUnit4.class)
public class EncryptedKeyTest extends TestCase {
    private final Gson gson = new Gson();

    private SecretKey generateKey(String algorithm) throws NoSuchAlgorithmException {
        KeyGenerator kg = KeyGenerator.getInstance(algorithm);
        kg.init(256);
        return kg.generateKey();
    }

    private String serialize(EncryptedKey encryptedKey) {
        return gson.toJson(encryptedKey);
    }

    private EncryptedKey deserialize(String serializedRecord) {
        return gson.fromJson(serializedRecord, EncryptedKey.class);
    }

    @Test
    public void encryptDecryptPreservesEncodedKeyAndAlgorithm()
            throws GeneralSecurityException, IOException {
        SecretKey plaintextKey = generateKey("HmacSHA512");
        SecretKey encryptionKey = generateKey("AES");

        EncryptedKey encryptedKey = EncryptedKey.encrypt(encryptionKey, plaintextKey);
        SecretKey decryptedKey = encryptedKey.decrypt(encryptionKey);

        Assert.assertArrayEquals(plaintextKey.getEncoded(), decryptedKey.getEncoded());
        assertEquals(plaintextKey.getAlgorithm(), decryptedKey.getAlgorithm());
    }

    @Test
    public void serializedRecordRetainsDataNeededForAadBoundDecryption()
            throws GeneralSecurityException, IOException {
        SecretKey plaintextKey = generateKey("HmacSHA512");
        SecretKey encryptionKey = generateKey("AES");

        EncryptedKey encryptedKey = EncryptedKey.encrypt(encryptionKey, plaintextKey);
        String serializedRecord = serialize(encryptedKey);
        EncryptedKey restoredRecord = deserialize(serializedRecord);
        SecretKey decryptedKey = restoredRecord.decrypt(encryptionKey);

        Assert.assertFalse(serializedRecord.isEmpty());
        Assert.assertArrayEquals(plaintextKey.getEncoded(), decryptedKey.getEncoded());
        assertEquals(plaintextKey.getAlgorithm(), decryptedKey.getAlgorithm());
    }

    @Test
    public void repeatedEncryptionUsesDistinctPersistedGcmParameters()
            throws GeneralSecurityException, IOException {
        SecretKey plaintextKey = generateKey("HmacSHA512");
        SecretKey encryptionKey = generateKey("AES");

        EncryptedKey firstRecord = EncryptedKey.encrypt(encryptionKey, plaintextKey);
        EncryptedKey secondRecord = EncryptedKey.encrypt(encryptionKey, plaintextKey);
        String firstSerializedRecord = serialize(firstRecord);
        String secondSerializedRecord = serialize(secondRecord);

        Assert.assertFalse(firstSerializedRecord.equals(secondSerializedRecord));
        Assert.assertArrayEquals(
                plaintextKey.getEncoded(),
                deserialize(firstSerializedRecord).decrypt(encryptionKey).getEncoded());
        Assert.assertArrayEquals(
                plaintextKey.getEncoded(),
                deserialize(secondSerializedRecord).decrypt(encryptionKey).getEncoded());
    }

    @Test
    public void utf8EncodedKeyRoundTrips() throws GeneralSecurityException, IOException {
        String plaintext = "火尸木火1十寥日烤";
        SecretKey encryptionKey = generateKey("AES");
        SecretKey plaintextKey = new SecretKeySpec(
                plaintext.getBytes(StandardCharsets.UTF_8), "AES");

        EncryptedKey encryptedKey = EncryptedKey.encrypt(encryptionKey, plaintextKey);
        SecretKey decryptedKey = encryptedKey.decrypt(encryptionKey);
        String decryptedText = new String(decryptedKey.getEncoded(), StandardCharsets.UTF_8);

        assertEquals(plaintext, decryptedText);
    }
}
